  "server": "infra/docker/streaming-stt app.py as the GPU image runs it: STT_PROVIDER=cuda, STT_MAX_SESSIONS=8, defaults otherwise (2 CPU threads, STT_PAD_MS=500 for whole-utterance models on CUDA, STT_FINALIZE_PAD_MS=600 for Nemotron, STT_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0); one server process per model, on 127.0.0.1",
  "nemotron_export": "full-precision sherpa-onnx exports (csukuangfj2/...-560ms-2026-04-25 @ d655d5f6, ...-160ms-2026-04-25 @ 9660703a) registered as CUDA variants of nemotron-en-560 / -160 for the measurement (fp32_nemotron.py); the packaged int8 exports were also run on CUDA (short pass)",
  "parakeet_export": "parakeet-0.6b-v3-fp32 (CUDA_VARIANTS), as deployed",
  "client": "ws_client.py: the voice service's Deepgram live-listen query (linear16, interim_results=true, endpointing=100), 20 ms frames in real time, Finalize 0.2 s after the speech ends (its VAD stop_secs), CloseStream after the final; non-realtime for the WER passes (as fast as the server takes it)",
  "final_after_speech_ms": "last speech frame (10 ms frames above -35 dB of the peak) -> the final that answered Finalize",
  "stable_partial_after_speech_ms": "last speech frame -> the earliest interim (live words) from which every later interim already read as the final, after normalisation; partial_had_final_words counts the clips where such an interim existed (the voice service could act on it)",
  "concurrency": "4 real-time streams at once, 3 rounds, clips of up to 12 s from LibriSpeech test-clean and EdAcc (16 kHz and 8 kHz), each starting 0-2 s apart; nvidia-smi sampled every 250 ms",
